Holiday tables and validation fixtures contain factual calendar dates and
independently computed reference results. Calendar identities, verified and
projected horizons, primary sources, and the pinned development reference
implementations are documented in SPEC.md and validation/oracle.json.

The development oracle uses QuantLib, FinancePy, Python holidays and supporting
Python packages. The Rust library does not bundle or link these implementations;
it has no runtime dependencies. No upstream implementation source is vendored.
